<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(Introduction)/E(Introduction)/Pg 9 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

553 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(1.1 PURPOSE)/E(1.1 PURPOSE)/Pg 9 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

554 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/T(The Town of Candor Comprehensive Plan is a collaborative initiative undertaken in partnership with the Town of Candor Planning Board and Design Connect at Cornell University. This Plan aims to revisit and revitalize the town's planning strategies by building upon the foundation set in the 2016 Comprehensive Plan. This revision process will ensure that the plan remains relevant, addressing the evolving needs and aspirations of the town's population. )/E(The Town of Candor Comprehensive Plan is a collaborative initiative undertaken in partnership with the Town of Candor Planning Board and Design Connect at Cornell University. This Plan aims to revisit and revitalize the town's planning strategies by building upon the foundation set in the 2016 Comprehensive Plan. This revision process will ensure that the plan remains relevant, addressing the evolving needs and aspirations of the town's population. )/Pg 9 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

555 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(1.2 ABOUT THE COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/E(1.2 ABOUT THE COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 9 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

556 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(1.2.1 NEW YORK STATE STATUTES)/E(1.2.1 NEW YORK STATE STATUTES)/Pg 9 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

557 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/T(New York State law allows local governments to develop comprehensive plans, recognizing that critical decisions impacting communities are predominantly made at the local level. The authority to engage in comprehensive planning is one of the key powers given to local authorities by the state. The definition of a comprehensive plan in New York, along with its potential components and the procedures for its creation and adoption, are outlined in Town Law \247272-a. While local governments have the choice to adopt a comprehensive plan, it is not mandatory. However, it is required by New York law that all land use regulations align with the comprehensive plan, if one is adopted. Ensuring land use regulations are consistent with a current comprehensive plan offers substantial legal protection for these regulations. )/E(New York State law allows local governments to develop comprehensive plans, recognizing that critical decisions impacting communities are predominantly made at the local level. The authority to engage in comprehensive planning is one of the key powers given to local authorities by the state. The definition of a comprehensive plan in New York, along with its potential components and the procedures for its creation and adoption, are outlined in Town Law \247272-a. While local governments have the choice to adopt a comprehensive plan, it is not mandatory. However, it is required by New York law that all land use regulations align with the comprehensive plan, if one is adopted. Ensuring land use regulations are consistent with a current comprehensive plan offers substantial legal protection for these regulations. )/Pg 9 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

558 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(1.2.2 WHY THE PLAN DIFFERS FROM ZONING)/E(1.2.2 WHY THE PLAN DIFFERS FROM ZONING)/Pg 9 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

559 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1671 0 R/ActualText(Scope: A comprehensive plan, like the one for the Town of Candor, is a broad, long-term plan that guides the overall development and growth of a community. It encompasses a wide range of elements such as land use, housing, transportation, economic development, natural resources, and community welfare.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

560 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1672 0 R/ActualText(Focus: This plan is visionary and strategic, focusing on the community's goals, aspirations, and desired future state. It includes public input and considers various aspects of community life.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

561 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1673 0 R/ActualText(Zoning: Zoning is a set of regulations that implement the comprehensive plan's vision at a more detailed and enforceable level. It specifically governs land use, building sizes, types of buildings, densities, and the layout of development within different zones of the town.)/Pg 9 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

562 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 9 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

