<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(04)/Pg 11 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

580 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(the dissolution referendum by a vote of 165 - 70, likely due to some of these aforementioned issues. Therefore, services remain separate between the Village and the Town except where cooperation already exists. )/E(the dissolution referendum by a vote of 165 - 70, likely due to some of these aforementioned issues. Therefore, services remain separate between the Village and the Town except where cooperation already exists. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

581 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(This is a Comprehensive Plan for the Town of Candor. Nonetheless, the Village of Candor is indisputably both a geographic and community center. Additionally, as residents of the Village are also Town residents, this Comprehensive Plan makes recommendations to improve the well-being of all residents. As the Village and Town are still separate, some local concerns should be addressed through communication and partnership between the two levels of government. )/E(This is a Comprehensive Plan for the Town of Candor. Nonetheless, the Village of Candor is indisputably both a geographic and community center. Additionally, as residents of the Village are also Town residents, this Comprehensive Plan makes recommendations to improve the well-being of all residents. As the Village and Town are still separate, some local concerns should be addressed through communication and partnership between the two levels of government. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

582 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(1.3.3 HIGHLIGHTING SUCCESS OF LIVING IN CANDOR)/E(1.3.3 HIGHLIGHTING SUCCESS OF LIVING IN CANDOR)/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

583 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Recent improvements to the Town of Candor are aimed at improving the quality of life, both inside and outside the Village. )/E(Recent improvements to the Town of Candor are aimed at improving the quality of life, both inside and outside the Village. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

584 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(For example, The Tioga County Property Development Corporation, a New York State Land Bank, was awarded a Main Street Revitalization grant for $500,000 to rehabilitate three buildings on Main street in the Village of Candor. The grant will bring life to formerly underutilized historic buildings and enhance Main Street by providing new shopping opportunities for nearby residents in Candor. This renovation is also leading to the opening of a new grocery store, Mama O\220s, and Two Brothers Pizza and Subs. )/E(For example, The Tioga County Property Development Corporation, a New York State Land Bank, was awarded a Main Street Revitalization grant for $500,000 to rehabilitate three buildings on Main street in the Village of Candor. The grant will bring life to formerly underutilized historic buildings and enhance Main Street by providing new shopping opportunities for nearby residents in Candor. This renovation is also leading to the opening of a new grocery store, Mama O\220s, and Two Brothers Pizza and Subs. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

585 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Additionally, the Town recently faced a crisis: volunteers formerly working at Candor EMS were becoming unable to meet the demands of the job, especially as they aged and the community dealt with the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020. Without the volunteer base needed to support this critical health service, the EMS was at risk of becoming unable to support local residents. This is a problem faced by communities across the country, but the Town Board was willing to create a new municipal ambulance service and cover some of the operating costs of that service. Since creating paid positions on the Candor Emergency Squad, membership has jumped from just 13 volunteers and 3 to 4 part-time paramedics in 2019 to 25 paid staff, 6 volunteers, and 6 active junior members in 2023. Under the leadership of Chief Curtis Hammond, Candor EMS has won hundreds of thousands of dollars in grants to support programs and equipment. They recover their costs through Town tax revenue earmarked for payroll and billing revenue they receive when responding to calls \(as well as grants and fundraising to support operations\). The EMS has largely been well-received by the community and is located in the heart of the Village of Candor, where they have an open door policy to provide support to anybody who walks through the door. )/E(Additionally, the Town recently faced a crisis: volunteers formerly working at Candor EMS were becoming unable to meet the demands of the job, especially as they aged and the community dealt with the COVID-19 pandemic in 2020. Without the volunteer base needed to support this critical health service, the EMS was at risk of becoming unable to support local residents. This is a problem faced by communities across the country, but the Town Board was willing to create a new municipal ambulance service and cover some of the operating costs of that service. Since creating paid positions on the Candor Emergency Squad, membership has jumped from just 13 volunteers and 3 to 4 part-time paramedics in 2019 to 25 paid staff, 6 volunteers, and 6 active junior members in 2023. Under the leadership of Chief Curtis Hammond, Candor EMS has won hundreds of thousands of dollars in grants to support programs and equipment. They recover their costs through Town tax revenue earmarked for payroll and billing revenue they receive when responding to calls \(as well as grants and fundraising to support operations\). The EMS has largely been well-received by the community and is located in the heart of the Village of Candor, where they have an open door policy to provide support to anybody who walks through the door. )/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

586 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 12 0 R/K[3]>>
