endobj

599 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1674 0 R/ActualText(Knowledge is Empowerment: Familiarize yourself with this document and its contents, and ensure any local groups or associations you're involved in do the same.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

600 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1675 0 R/ActualText(Active Involvement: Volunteer in planning events aligned with this plan, set Candor-centric goals, and collaborate with those responsible for relevant tasks to overcome resource limitations.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

601 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1676 0 R/ActualText(Local Investment: Rally together to invest in Candor's small businesses and kickstart projects that rejuvenate buildings or lots, keeping investments local rather than waiting for external developers.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

602 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1677 0 R/ActualText(Participation in Reviews: Engage in the Town of Candor's plan reviews to propose innovative ideas and make leaders aware of evolving community needs.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

603 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1678 0 R/ActualText(Collective Accountability: Recognize that progress discussions involve both city officials and residents. Contribute to and celebrate achievements, and partake in constructive assessments of shortcomings.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

604 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(For Officials of Candor:)/E(For Officials of Candor:)/Pg 14 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

605 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1679 0 R/ActualText(Plan Alignment: Ensure that Candor's budget, regulations, and agendas are in sync with the plan\220s goals.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

606 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1680 0 R/ActualText(Facilitating Resident Participation: Make it easy for residents and local groups to contribute to achieving Candor's vision.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

607 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1681 0 R/ActualText(Dialogue Around the Plan: Use the plan as a reference in city discussions, setting an example of commitment to Candor's future.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

608 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1682 0 R/ActualText(Regular Review and Update: Maintain an annual review of the plan, policies, and regulations to ensure they remain relevant and reflect the community's changing needs.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

609 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1683 0 R/ActualText(Accessibility and Transparency: Share the plan widely and demonstrate its application in decision-making to help residents understand the connection between vision and action.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

610 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1684 0 R/ActualText(Vision-Led Decisions: Use the plan as a guideline for evaluating special projects or development opportunities.)/Pg 14 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

611 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 14 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

612 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(07)/Pg 14 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

613 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(PART 2)/E(PART 2)/Pg 15 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

614 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(Community Priorities)/E(Community Priorities)/Pg 15 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

615 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(2.1 LAND USE AND INFRA)/E(2.1 LAND USE AND INFRA)/Pg 15 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

616 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(LU)/E(LU)/Pg 15 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

617 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This theme focuses on the planning and management of physical spaces within the community. It encompasses the distribution of different land uses, such as residential, commercial, industrial, and recreational areas. Infrastructure considerations include transportation networks and public facilities. The goal is to create a balanced, sustainable environment that meets the community's current and future needs.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

618 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(2.3 COMMUNITY WELFARE)/E(2.3 COMMUNITY WELFARE)/Pg 15 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

619 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H6/T(CW)/E(CW)/Pg 15 0 R/K[19]>>
endobj

620 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Community welfare encompasses the overall health, well-being, and quality of life of the residents. This includes access to healthcare, education, cultural activities, and community services. It also involves ensuring equity and inclusion, addressing social needs, and fostering a sense of community and belonging among residents.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

621 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(2.5 PUBLIC SAFETY)/E(2.5 PUBLIC SAFETY)/Pg 15 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

622 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(PS)/E(PS)/Pg 15 0 R/K[21]>>
endobj

623 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Public safety is concerned with protecting the community from risks and hazards. This includes effective law enforcement, fire services, and emergency management. It also involves community-based approaches to safety, such as neighborhood watch programs and public safety education. The goal is to create a secure environment where residents feel safe and protected.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

624 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(2.2 GOVERNANCE)/E(2.2 GOVERNANCE)/Pg 15 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

625 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(GV)/E(GV)/Pg 15 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

626 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Governance relates to how the community is managed and the processes through which decisions are made. This includes the effectiveness and transparency of local government, community involvement in decision-making, and the implementation of policies and regulations. It emphasizes the need for responsive, accountable leadership that actively engages with and serves the interests of its citizens.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

627 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(2.4 NATURAL RESOURCES)/E(2.4 NATURAL RESOURCES)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

628 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(NR)/E(NR)/Pg 15 0 R/K[18]>>
endobj

629 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(This theme focuses on the conservation and sustainable management of natural resources such as water bodies, parks, and forests. It involves protecting ecosystems, promoting biodiversity, and ensuring that natural assets are preserved for future generations. It also covers aspects like green space accessibility, environmental education, and sustainable practices to mitigate climate change impacts.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

630 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(2.6 ECONOMIC GROWTH)/E(2.6 ECONOMIC GROWTH)/Pg 15 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

631 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(EG)/E(EG)/Pg 15 0 R/K[20]>>
endobj

632 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(Sustainable economic growth balances immediate benefits with long-term well-being, avoiding environmental and social costs. It leads to higher living standards, including better income, health care, education, and access to amenities. Economic growth is integral to overall economic development, focusing on enhancing life quality and living conditions.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

633 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/T(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/E(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 15 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

