endobj

654 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(School District The majority of Candor town is covered by the Candor Central School District. It serves students in the Town and Village of Candor as well as parts of Owego to the South, Willseyvile to the North, and Broookstondale to the Northeast. It covers K-12 education including the two schools: Candor Elementary School and Candor Junior Senior High School combined. The remainder of the town attends other school districts in Newark Valley, Owego, Ithaca, Spencer/Van Etten, and Tioga districts. )/E(School District The majority of Candor town is covered by the Candor Central School District. It serves students in the Town and Village of Candor as well as parts of Owego to the South, Willseyvile to the North, and Broookstondale to the Northeast. It covers K-12 education including the two schools: Candor Elementary School and Candor Junior Senior High School combined. The remainder of the town attends other school districts in Newark Valley, Owego, Ithaca, Spencer/Van Etten, and Tioga districts. )/Pg 18 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

655 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Higher Education For higher education, the town is linked and at a vital location to multiple colleges and universities. Candor residents enjoy outstanding academic accessibility to institutions of higher learning such as Cornell University, Binghamton University, SUNY Cortland, Ithaca College, and TC3 \(Tompkins Cortland Community College\). )/E(Higher Education For higher education, the town is linked and at a vital location to multiple colleges and universities. Candor residents enjoy outstanding academic accessibility to institutions of higher learning such as Cornell University, Binghamton University, SUNY Cortland, Ithaca College, and TC3 \(Tompkins Cortland Community College\). )/Pg 18 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

656 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Overall, there is majority of the population completes a high school degree. The 2020 census shows that over 90% of the population over the age of 25 are high school graduates or higher. However, only 12.2% of the population has received a Bachelor's degree or a graduate degree, a relatively low percentage compared to Tioga County\220s average percentage of 25.8% and Owego Town\220s 38.1% of the population receiving a Bachelor\220s degree or higher.)/E(Overall, there is majority of the population completes a high school degree. The 2020 census shows that over 90% of the population over the age of 25 are high school graduates or higher. However, only 12.2% of the population has received a Bachelor's degree or a graduate degree, a relatively low percentage compared to Tioga County\220s average percentage of 25.8% and Owego Town\220s 38.1% of the population receiving a Bachelor\220s degree or higher.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

657 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(3.1.4 AGE DISTRIBUTION)/E(3.1.4 AGE DISTRIBUTION)/Pg 18 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

