<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 18 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

660 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(11)/Pg 18 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

661 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(3.1.5 INCOME AND POVERTY)/E(3.1.5 INCOME AND POVERTY)/Pg 19 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

662 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(The median household income \(in 2021 dollars\) for the town of Candor is $48,157. In comparison the county\220s overall median income of $64,987\(\261$ 1,996\) according to ACS\220s 5-year estimate in 2021. There is a Per capita income of $30,500 and a poverty percentage of %16.6. The town has an overall lower median income as well as a higher poverty rate than the county\220s average of 11.7%. This could be due to the high portion of the senior population \(65 years old and higher\) in town as more people have retired from full-time employment. )/E(The median household income \(in 2021 dollars\) for the town of Candor is $48,157. In comparison the county\220s overall median income of $64,987\(\261$ 1,996\) according to ACS\220s 5-year estimate in 2021. There is a Per capita income of $30,500 and a poverty percentage of %16.6. The town has an overall lower median income as well as a higher poverty rate than the county\220s average of 11.7%. This could be due to the high portion of the senior population \(65 years old and higher\) in town as more people have retired from full-time employment. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

663 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(3.1.6 WORKFORCE )/E(3.1.6 WORKFORCE )/Pg 19 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

664 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(The town has a 55.6% employment rate which is lower than the county\220s employment rate of 57.4%. According to ACS\220s 2021 5-year estimate, The majority of the Candor population works in the management in business, science, and arts occupations \(27.4%\), second being sales and office occupations \(23.4%\), other works in health care social services sectors. More details are included in Part 5 \(Economic Development\) of the plan.)/E(The town has a 55.6% employment rate which is lower than the county\220s employment rate of 57.4%. According to ACS\220s 2021 5-year estimate, The majority of the Candor population works in the management in business, science, and arts occupations \(27.4%\), second being sales and office occupations \(23.4%\), other works in health care social services sectors. More details are included in Part 5 \(Economic Development\) of the plan.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

665 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(3.1.7 HOUSEHOLD SIZES)/E(3.1.7 HOUSEHOLD SIZES)/Pg 19 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

666 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(There are 1,663 households in the Town of Candor. \(USThe average household size is 2.17 persons per household. This is lower than the state average of 2.69 persons per household. This data is expected due to the overall lower density in demography. The median value of owner-occupied housing units for Candor Town is $128.700 compared to the State\220s $340,600, which is about 3 times lower. Of these households, 88.9% has broadband internet subscription as well as a high percentage of 94.2% of households that owns a computer. Both data are higher than the state average indicating the higher accessibility to technology within town. More details are recorded in Part 6 \(Household\) of the plan. )/E(There are 1,663 households in the Town of Candor. \(USThe average household size is 2.17 persons per household. This is lower than the state average of 2.69 persons per household. This data is expected due to the overall lower density in demography. The median value of owner-occupied housing units for Candor Town is $128.700 compared to the State\220s $340,600, which is about 3 times lower. Of these households, 88.9% has broadband internet subscription as well as a high percentage of 94.2% of households that owns a computer. Both data are higher than the state average indicating the higher accessibility to technology within town. More details are recorded in Part 6 \(Household\) of the plan. )/Pg 19 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

