<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/T(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/E(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 23 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

784 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(16)/Pg 23 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

785 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(Additionally, much of the vacant land can be attributed to \215Rural Vacant,\216 both greater than and less than 10 acres, which combined are responsible for nearly 63% of all vacancies in Candor. However, that\220s not to overlook the high counts of vacant residential and vacancies with improvements within Candor. There is also a high prevalence of agricultural and natural spaces, aligning with Candor\220s pastoral culture and organic resources. )/E(Additionally, much of the vacant land can be attributed to \215Rural Vacant,\216 both greater than and less than 10 acres, which combined are responsible for nearly 63% of all vacancies in Candor. However, that\220s not to overlook the high counts of vacant residential and vacancies with improvements within Candor. There is also a high prevalence of agricultural and natural spaces, aligning with Candor\220s pastoral culture and organic resources. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

786 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 465 0 R/Pg 24 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

787 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(Data Source: NYSGIS, 2023)/E(Data Source: NYSGIS, 2023)/Pg 24 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

788 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(Together, the three uses of Residential, Mixed Use, and Vacant account for over 86% of all parcels within Candor. Contrastingly, commercial uses were only identified as a miniscule total 1.11% of Candor. This distinct lack of commercial spaces seems to be near population centers, at least in the Village of Candor, West Candor, and Willseyville. The areas surrounding Highway 96, 96B, and Mill Street are all mainly residential areas or vacant \(with the exception of the intersection between 96B and Mill Street\). )/E(Together, the three uses of Residential, Mixed Use, and Vacant account for over 86% of all parcels within Candor. Contrastingly, commercial uses were only identified as a miniscule total 1.11% of Candor. This distinct lack of commercial spaces seems to be near population centers, at least in the Village of Candor, West Candor, and Willseyville. The areas surrounding Highway 96, 96B, and Mill Street are all mainly residential areas or vacant \(with the exception of the intersection between 96B and Mill Street\). )/Pg 24 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

789 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(For regular residential uses, they also all appear to follow roads, either local or major ones. Lastly, within the Village of Candor, there are a variety of services and uses available, including numerous recreational opportunities, health services, and a police or fire station. However, this singular usage of for health within the Village was the only one of its kind near population centers in Candor. Furthermore, the village also contains the only notable usage for School in the town of Candor. Lastly, it is valuable to recognize the vast amounts of vacant parcels that aren\220t attributed to \215Rural Vacant,\216 as in the lots along the main streets within the Village of Candor that should be considered for development. )/E(For regular residential uses, they also all appear to follow roads, either local or major ones. Lastly, within the Village of Candor, there are a variety of services and uses available, including numerous recreational opportunities, health services, and a police or fire station. However, this singular usage of for health within the Village was the only one of its kind near population centers in Candor. Furthermore, the village also contains the only notable usage for School in the town of Candor. Lastly, it is valuable to recognize the vast amounts of vacant parcels that aren\220t attributed to \215Rural Vacant,\216 as in the lots along the main streets within the Village of Candor that should be considered for development. )/Pg 24 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

790 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 24 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

791 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(17)/Pg 24 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

792 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(4.1.3 LAND USE ANALYSIS)/E(4.1.3 LAND USE ANALYSIS)/Pg 25 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

793 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Given these land use patterns, several recommendations can be made regarding the best approach to continue developing the usage of Candor. Firstly, encouraging more commercial development along key corridors rather than residential spaces would significantly benefit the possibility of business retention given their greater access to customers and visitors. None of the areas depicted outside of Germany Hill showcased notable commercial areas along its major roads and intersections.)/E(Given these land use patterns, several recommendations can be made regarding the best approach to continue developing the usage of Candor. Firstly, encouraging more commercial development along key corridors rather than residential spaces would significantly benefit the possibility of business retention given their greater access to customers and visitors. None of the areas depicted outside of Germany Hill showcased notable commercial areas along its major roads and intersections.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

794 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Nonetheless, there are an overwhelming amount of empty and vacant lots along these highways which can be utilized to both reduce eyesore while incentivizing development. The greater establishment of improvements along these lots would also facilitate the possibility of subsequent implementation of other supportive infrastructural improvements such as sidewalks or street lights. Additionally, this is something that would not take away from that rural character of Candor as it does not recommend the development of those mixed-use \215Rural Residential and Agricultural Use[s]\216 nor the \215Rural Vacant\216 uses.  )/E(Nonetheless, there are an overwhelming amount of empty and vacant lots along these highways which can be utilized to both reduce eyesore while incentivizing development. The greater establishment of improvements along these lots would also facilitate the possibility of subsequent implementation of other supportive infrastructural improvements such as sidewalks or street lights. Additionally, this is something that would not take away from that rural character of Candor as it does not recommend the development of those mixed-use \215Rural Residential and Agricultural Use[s]\216 nor the \215Rural Vacant\216 uses.  )/Pg 25 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

795 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(4.1.4 PROPERTY TAX REVENUE)/E(4.1.4 PROPERTY TAX REVENUE)/Pg 25 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

796 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Property taxes serve as Candor\220s main source of revenue, with over 85% of its annual income in the budget coming from so. The tax revenue for Candor in both the village and the town have increased steadily over the last decade. Starting at $226,336,861 for the town in 2014, Candor\220s tax revenue in 2022 reached $241,416,678 with an increase of over $15 million. Similarly during this time frame, both Tioga County as a whole and the Village of Candor have seen similar increases, with $15 million as well and over $400,000 respectively.  Additionally, from 2014-2022 Candor has gained nearly 100 more taxable parcels, rising from 2,783 to 2,878. Overall, there aren\220t any large fluctuations or changes for Candor\220s tax revenue on a year to year basis, however it is clear property tax revenue has grown consistently over the last ten years. )/E(Property taxes serve as Candor\220s main source of revenue, with over 85% of its annual income in the budget coming from so. The tax revenue for Candor in both the village and the town have increased steadily over the last decade. Starting at $226,336,861 for the town in 2014, Candor\220s tax revenue in 2022 reached $241,416,678 with an increase of over $15 million. Similarly during this time frame, both Tioga County as a whole and the Village of Candor have seen similar increases, with $15 million as well and over $400,000 respectively.  Additionally, from 2014-2022 Candor has gained nearly 100 more taxable parcels, rising from 2,783 to 2,878. Overall, there aren\220t any large fluctuations or changes for Candor\220s tax revenue on a year to year basis, however it is clear property tax revenue has grown consistently over the last ten years. )/Pg 25 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

