<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/T(Candor has an average occupancy rate and vacancy rate at approximately the count average. The owner occupancy rate is 5% lower compared to the county average, while the renter occupancy rate is 5% higher. 66 homes are owned with a mortgage or a loan, and 804 are owned free and clear \(2020 Census\). Of vacant properties, 26 are for rent, 2 are rented but not occupied, 14 are for sale only, 41 are sold but not occupied, 56 are for seasonal, recreational, or occasional use, and 60 are classified as \215other vacant\216 \(2020 Census\). )/E(Candor has an average occupancy rate and vacancy rate at approximately the count average. The owner occupancy rate is 5% lower compared to the county average, while the renter occupancy rate is 5% higher. 66 homes are owned with a mortgage or a loan, and 804 are owned free and clear \(2020 Census\). Of vacant properties, 26 are for rent, 2 are rented but not occupied, 14 are for sale only, 41 are sold but not occupied, 56 are for seasonal, recreational, or occasional use, and 60 are classified as \215other vacant\216 \(2020 Census\). )/Pg 38 0 R/K[65]>>
