endobj

1053 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Candor offers many sport facilities for outdoor recreation, both privately owned, and those owned by the town. These include the Candor Little League Baseball field, the Candor softball field, the American Legion horseshoe fields, Robinson, Ward and Fire Hall soccer fields, and Candor school sports fields. In addition, there are snowmobile and all-vehicle club trails within the Town which are heavily supported by the town\220s residents. )/E(Candor offers many sport facilities for outdoor recreation, both privately owned, and those owned by the town. These include the Candor Little League Baseball field, the Candor softball field, the American Legion horseshoe fields, Robinson, Ward and Fire Hall soccer fields, and Candor school sports fields. In addition, there are snowmobile and all-vehicle club trails within the Town which are heavily supported by the town\220s residents. )/Pg 42 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1054 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(There are two trail systems in Candor. Right outside the village of Candor is the Logan Nature Preserve Trail, which includes the Aspen Campground. )/E(There are two trail systems in Candor. Right outside the village of Candor is the Logan Nature Preserve Trail, which includes the Aspen Campground. )/Pg 42 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1055 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Candor also offers a limited number of commercial recreational facilities, such as the Catatonk Golf Club, which is located in the southwestern part of Candor and offers an 18-hole golf course in addition to a 350-acre multipurpose event space. )/E(Candor also offers a limited number of commercial recreational facilities, such as the Catatonk Golf Club, which is located in the southwestern part of Candor and offers an 18-hole golf course in addition to a 350-acre multipurpose event space. )/Pg 42 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1056 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(As a rural agricultural community, many local farms within Candor also offer seasonal recreational activities for residents and visitors. Side Hill Acres Farm, located at 79 Spencer Road, provides farm tours as well as events during seasonal festivals in the community. Hilltop Community Farm, part of the Cornell Cooperative Extension of Tioga County, is located at Cass Hill Road in Candor and provides multiple educational and explorative opportunities for people of all ages. The farm has recently also developed a play space for youth, which began installment in summer 2023. )/E(As a rural agricultural community, many local farms within Candor also offer seasonal recreational activities for residents and visitors. Side Hill Acres Farm, located at 79 Spencer Road, provides farm tours as well as events during seasonal festivals in the community. Hilltop Community Farm, part of the Cornell Cooperative Extension of Tioga County, is located at Cass Hill Road in Candor and provides multiple educational and explorative opportunities for people of all ages. The farm has recently also developed a play space for youth, which began installment in summer 2023. )/Pg 42 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1057 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(TOWN OF CANDOR - COMPREHENSIVE PLAN)/Pg 42 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

1058 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/ActualText(35)/Pg 42 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

1059 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Conveniently located in Tioga County and a short distance away from Tompkins County, Candor is further easily accessible to many recreational offerings in neighboring towns. Both counties offer numerous hiking trails, parks, wildlife and preservation centers. )/E(Conveniently located in Tioga County and a short distance away from Tompkins County, Candor is further easily accessible to many recreational offerings in neighboring towns. Both counties offer numerous hiking trails, parks, wildlife and preservation centers. )/Pg 43 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1060 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Candor sits alongside the Catatonk Creek, which comes into the village from the northwest and passes through Main Street down south towards Hubbardtown and ends in Owego, NY.  Currently, the Creek does not provide any dedication space for recreation. The majority of the land surrounding the southern portion of the Creek in the village is owned by the Candor School System and central parts are owned by the Candor Fire District. The rest of the creek\220s surrounding land is privately owned as well, except for a small portion in the northwest of the Candor, which is owned by the Town. This area, in consultation with the adjacent landowners, could have prospects for some type of waterfront development for recreational uses and access links to other trail systems in the Finger Lakes area. It is adamant that these developments or consultations do not infringe on the rights of the property owners within Candor. )/E(Candor sits alongside the Catatonk Creek, which comes into the village from the northwest and passes through Main Street down south towards Hubbardtown and ends in Owego, NY.  Currently, the Creek does not provide any dedication space for recreation. The majority of the land surrounding the southern portion of the Creek in the village is owned by the Candor School System and central parts are owned by the Candor Fire District. The rest of the creek\220s surrounding land is privately owned as well, except for a small portion in the northwest of the Candor, which is owned by the Town. This area, in consultation with the adjacent landowners, could have prospects for some type of waterfront development for recreational uses and access links to other trail systems in the Finger Lakes area. It is adamant that these developments or consultations do not infringe on the rights of the property owners within Candor. )/Pg 43 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1061 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(7.1.3 SOLAR ENERGY SYSTEMS)/E(7.1.3 SOLAR ENERGY SYSTEMS)/Pg 43 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1062 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Candor prides itself in its agricultural history and agricultural land offerings. In addition to its practical argiucltural uses, and recreational use, open space presents a great resource for solar energy development, which has become a contested topic across the upstate New York region. Since its last comprehensive plan, the Town of Candor has committed to preserving the most productive land for active agricultural use. Since then, the Candor Planning Board has also been developing and rewriting local laws to help regulate the presence and look of solar energy systems on land within the town. )/E(Candor prides itself in its agricultural history and agricultural land offerings. In addition to its practical argiucltural uses, and recreational use, open space presents a great resource for solar energy development, which has become a contested topic across the upstate New York region. Since its last comprehensive plan, the Town of Candor has committed to preserving the most productive land for active agricultural use. Since then, the Candor Planning Board has also been developing and rewriting local laws to help regulate the presence and look of solar energy systems on land within the town. )/Pg 43 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

