endobj

1065 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(7.1.4 TOWN PARK PROPOSAL)/E(7.1.4 TOWN PARK PROPOSAL)/Pg 44 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

1066 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Our inventory analysis found that Candor currently has minimal recreation offerings for its population \(taking into account both indoor and outdoor facilities\). After conducting our community based survey with the residents of Candor, we found that many residents desired more recreation spaces within Candor\205particularly for families with younger children and for senior citizens. Based upon our conducted research, roughly 18% of Candor\220s residents are elderly citizens, and many of the town\220s current streets either lack signage or are not pedestrian-friendly. The current park and fields within the town are affiliated with the Candor school system, which leaves them not entirely accessible to non-school affiliates. For these reasons, there is a need for a community space that will not only provide offerings for a wide range of people, but also facilitate unity by bringing them together. )/E(Our inventory analysis found that Candor currently has minimal recreation offerings for its population \(taking into account both indoor and outdoor facilities\). After conducting our community based survey with the residents of Candor, we found that many residents desired more recreation spaces within Candor\205particularly for families with younger children and for senior citizens. Based upon our conducted research, roughly 18% of Candor\220s residents are elderly citizens, and many of the town\220s current streets either lack signage or are not pedestrian-friendly. The current park and fields within the town are affiliated with the Candor school system, which leaves them not entirely accessible to non-school affiliates. For these reasons, there is a need for a community space that will not only provide offerings for a wide range of people, but also facilitate unity by bringing them together. )/Pg 44 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1067 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(In 2018, the Candor planning board, in collaboration with Cornell University\220s Design Connect, produced a proposal for a community park to be located on approximately 3.5 acres of Town-owned land situated in Eastern Candor, between the Dollar General and Maple Grove Cemetery. )/E(In 2018, the Candor planning board, in collaboration with Cornell University\220s Design Connect, produced a proposal for a community park to be located on approximately 3.5 acres of Town-owned land situated in Eastern Candor, between the Dollar General and Maple Grove Cemetery. )/Pg 44 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1068 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 485 0 R/Pg 44 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

1069 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(With reference to the 2018 Town Park plan, and with input from both the planning board and community conducted survey, we have put together a proposal for a Candor Town Park to be implemented in the near future. )/E(With reference to the 2018 Town Park plan, and with input from both the planning board and community conducted survey, we have put together a proposal for a Candor Town Park to be implemented in the near future. )/Pg 44 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

