endobj

1083 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H5/T(Implementation of this proposal will necessitate further consultation between the Candor Planning Board, Candor Chamber of Commerce, third party consultation and contraction firms, in addition to the community members and further advisors as deemed fit. At the present time, there is a need to develop a concrete timeline for the progression of the community park. After the development of the 2018 proposal and positive reception from the community, advancement on the plan was stalled. After visiting the idea again in fall of 2023, the proposal was once again positive received and cited to fill a necessary gap within the community. For this reason, the first needed step is to understand why advancement on the Town Community Park proposal has not occurred between 2018 and 2023. The details of the 2018 proposal, which will be included in this plan\220s appendix, need to be revisited and reassessed by the involved actors. This reassessment should also include a reevaluation of the proposed park design and associated budget, which may result in design eliminations, minimizations, or an otherwise phased approach for development feasibility. If the main recognized barrier to the park\220s development is identified as financial, the next needed measure should be identifying accessible funding opportunities, which may include grants, private collaborators, or crowdfunding initiatives, as deemed appropriate by the involved parties. Once feasibility is better understood and determined, a commitment to development should be made. Members of the community should be consulted and timely updated on all aspects of the plan. )/E(Implementation of this proposal will necessitate further consultation between the Candor Planning Board, Candor Chamber of Commerce, third party consultation and contraction firms, in addition to the community members and further advisors as deemed fit. At the present time, there is a need to develop a concrete timeline for the progression of the community park. After the development of the 2018 proposal and positive reception from the community, advancement on the plan was stalled. After visiting the idea again in fall of 2023, the proposal was once again positive received and cited to fill a necessary gap within the community. For this reason, the first needed step is to understand why advancement on the Town Community Park proposal has not occurred between 2018 and 2023. The details of the 2018 proposal, which will be included in this plan\220s appendix, need to be revisited and reassessed by the involved actors. This reassessment should also include a reevaluation of the proposed park design and associated budget, which may result in design eliminations, minimizations, or an otherwise phased approach for development feasibility. If the main recognized barrier to the park\220s development is identified as financial, the next needed measure should be identifying accessible funding opportunities, which may include grants, private collaborators, or crowdfunding initiatives, as deemed appropriate by the involved parties. Once feasibility is better understood and determined, a commitment to development should be made. Members of the community should be consulted and timely updated on all aspects of the plan. )/Pg 47 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

