1121 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(Of 378 total comments within the survey, 70 related to roads or speeding. 25 were about speeding, 5 were about trucks, and the remaining 40 were about road quality. Additionally, 8 mentioned Main Street by name, 4 mentioned Prospect Valley Road, 2 mentioned Honeypot Road, and 17 other roads were mentioned once, with 3 of which mentioning a specific road, but left it unnamed. )/E(Of 378 total comments within the survey, 70 related to roads or speeding. 25 were about speeding, 5 were about trucks, and the remaining 40 were about road quality. Additionally, 8 mentioned Main Street by name, 4 mentioned Prospect Valley Road, 2 mentioned Honeypot Road, and 17 other roads were mentioned once, with 3 of which mentioning a specific road, but left it unnamed. )/Pg 51 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1122 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(The primary concern within the responses pertained to road upkeep, with most comments consisting requests to upkeep both paved and seasonal roads. This is likely due to the Seasonal Roads Use Law \(2011\) which requires the town to only upkeep one mile of seasonal roads per calendar year. )/E(The primary concern within the responses pertained to road upkeep, with most comments consisting requests to upkeep both paved and seasonal roads. This is likely due to the Seasonal Roads Use Law \(2011\) which requires the town to only upkeep one mile of seasonal roads per calendar year. )/Pg 51 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1123 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H4/T(The secondary concern within the responses is safety, as due to the lack of sidewalks and reasonable average vehicle speed, residents tended to feel unsafe traversing by foot. This was accompanied by calls for a speed sheriff to enforce the speed limit.)/E(The secondary concern within the responses is safety, as due to the lack of sidewalks and reasonable average vehicle speed, residents tended to feel unsafe traversing by foot. This was accompanied by calls for a speed sheriff to enforce the speed limit.)/Pg 51 0 R/K[4]>>
