1143 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Volusias are generally poorly drained and moderately fertile. Depth to water table ranges from 24 to 80 inches, with \217elevated wetlands\220 in poorly drained and shallow areas. Many upland soil units are sloped and eroded, with fragipans or clay layers that aggravate soil nutrient leaching and runoff. )/E(Volusias are generally poorly drained and moderately fertile. Depth to water table ranges from 24 to 80 inches, with \217elevated wetlands\220 in poorly drained and shallow areas. Many upland soil units are sloped and eroded, with fragipans or clay layers that aggravate soil nutrient leaching and runoff. )/Pg 53 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1144 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(9.1.3 VEGETATION)/E(9.1.3 VEGETATION)/Pg 53 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1145 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Candor\220s vegetation is largely defined by temperate-climate deciduous forests, composed of Red Maple, Sugar Maple, Hemlock, White Ash, Black Cherry, and Northern Red Oak tree species. Fields and meadows feature cultivated crops, mixed native and introduced grasses, and mixed temperate woodland brush. )/E(Candor\220s vegetation is largely defined by temperate-climate deciduous forests, composed of Red Maple, Sugar Maple, Hemlock, White Ash, Black Cherry, and Northern Red Oak tree species. Fields and meadows feature cultivated crops, mixed native and introduced grasses, and mixed temperate woodland brush. )/Pg 53 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

