endobj

1169 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(enduring environmental impacts on soil and water quality. Large-scale projects in visible locations may finally compromise Candor\220s rural character and threaten undeveloped and natural lands. )/E(enduring environmental impacts on soil and water quality. Large-scale projects in visible locations may finally compromise Candor\220s rural character and threaten undeveloped and natural lands. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

1170 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(9.1.9 EXISTING NATURAL RESOURCES STRATEGIES)/E(9.1.9 EXISTING NATURAL RESOURCES STRATEGIES)/Pg 56 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

1171 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Existing conservation and natural resources strategies in the Town include conservation easements on privately-held land, often agricultural, fallow, or forested. Landowners can yield development rights to the Town for a certain period of time in exchange for tax credits for their land, allowing the Town to maintain undeveloped open space.   Local natural resources monitoring and planning is largely handled by the Tioga County Soil and Water Conservation District, which gathers and disseminates pertinent data, establishes county-wide conservation goals, and provides farms and landowners with land conservation and management resources. Its areas of responsibility include watershed management and water quality testing, agricultural and soils data collection, local data mapping, and grant and loan funding assistance. )/E(Existing conservation and natural resources strategies in the Town include conservation easements on privately-held land, often agricultural, fallow, or forested. Landowners can yield development rights to the Town for a certain period of time in exchange for tax credits for their land, allowing the Town to maintain undeveloped open space.   Local natural resources monitoring and planning is largely handled by the Tioga County Soil and Water Conservation District, which gathers and disseminates pertinent data, establishes county-wide conservation goals, and provides farms and landowners with land conservation and management resources. Its areas of responsibility include watershed management and water quality testing, agricultural and soils data collection, local data mapping, and grant and loan funding assistance. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

1172 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H1/T(9.1.10 COUNTY AGRICULTURAL PLAN RECOMMENDATIONS )/E(9.1.10 COUNTY AGRICULTURAL PLAN RECOMMENDATIONS )/Pg 56 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

1173 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(The 2015 Tioga County Agricultural Protection Plan outlines the county\220s local natural resources, information on current agricultural operations and trends, and makes recommendations to support and grow local agricultural production. Recommendations pertinent to Candor include: )/E(The 2015 Tioga County Agricultural Protection Plan outlines the county\220s local natural resources, information on current agricultural operations and trends, and makes recommendations to support and grow local agricultural production. Recommendations pertinent to Candor include: )/Pg 56 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

1174 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1828 0 R/ActualText(Encouraging local town governments to implement Right-to-Farm Laws: Right-to-Farm laws uphold the importance of agricultural production to a town\220s economy, open space, and rural character. They legally state producers\220 right to follow agricultural best practices and inform local residents, reducing producers\220 vulnerability to nuisance lawsuits. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

1175 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1829 0 R/ActualText(Supporting agricultural producers in obtaining federal, state and local grants for equipment and innovation: Use county and local resources - including staff and data - to support producers\220 grant applications. Disseminate information on existing funding resources to producers. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

1176 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1830 0 R/ActualText(Encouraging local town governments with significant agricultural resources to establish agriculture advisory committees to advise town boards on agriculturally-related issues. Encourage local agricultural producers to participate in town governance that impacts their operations. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

1177 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 1831 0 R/ActualText(Promoting the continuation of agricultural uses in flood zones to absorb flood forces. Protect valuable soils where possible and help producers mitigate the impacts of flooding on their lands. )/Pg 56 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

